# Supabase Configuration (Cortex)
#
# Cortex (Next.js) loads env only from ITS OWN directory: put these in
# apps/cortex/.env, not the repo root. See apps/cortex/README.md, which also
# explains why NOT to use apps/cortex/.env.local. The root .env is read only by
# the packages/db scripts (seed, verify-*).
#
# Deployed Cortex reads these from the Vercel project's Environment Variables.
# A cloud Claude Code session reads them from its environment settings. Use a
# DEV project's keys there, never production's secret key.
#
# Find these in: Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys.
#
# Project URL: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
#
# Publishable key (formerly the "anon" key). Format: sb_publishable_...
# Low-privilege, safe to expose in client/browser code. Subject to RLS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
#
# Secret key (formerly the "service_role" key). Format: sb_secret_...
# Full-privilege, bypasses RLS. SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never add a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix:
# that would ship it to the browser.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
